%S A139826 1,2,3,5,6,7,10,13,15,21,22,30,33,37,42,57,58,70,78,85,93,102,105,130,
%T A139826 133,165,177,190,210,253,273,330,345,357,385,462,1365
%N A139826 Squarefree idoneal numbers (A000926).
%C A139826 There is at most one additional term (Kani, Corollary 23). If it exists, it is > 7.75*10^19 (Elsenhans, Klüners, and Nicolae, Theorem 1). If the generalized Riemann hypothesis holds, there are no further terms. - _David Radcliffe_, Aug 22 2026
%H A139826 J. M. Borwein and K. K. S. Choi, <a href="https://projecteuclid.org/journals/experimental-mathematics/volume-9/issue-1/On-the-representations-of-xyyzzx/em/1046889597.full">On the Representations of xy+yz+zx</a>, Experimental Mathematics 9 (2000), 153-158.
%H A139826 Andreas-Stephan Elsenhans, Jürgen Klüners, and Florin Nicolae, <a href="https://doi.org/10.4064/aa180220-20-3">Imaginary quadratic number fields with class groups of small exponent</a>, Acta Arithmetica, 193 (2020), no. 3, 217-233. See also <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.02056">arXiv:1803.02056 [math.NT]</a>, 2018.
%H A139826 E. Kani, <a href="https://mast.queensu.ca/~kani/papers/idoneal.pdf">Idoneal numbers and some generalizations</a>, Ann. Sci. Math. Québec, 35 (2011), no. 2, 197-227.
%H A139826 P. J. Weinberger, <a href="https://eudml.org/doc/205148">Exponents of the class groups of complex quadratic fields</a>, Acta Arithmetica, 22 (1973), no. 2, 117-124.
